## 2. History and why this portfolio exists

**Timeline [D: Yuho26 P7 history table unless noted]**
- 1957: founded in Osaka as the independent Osaka factory of Teikoku Pharmaceutical (Teikoku Seiyaku, 帝國製薬). Early products: malic acid (food additive), later citric acid, gluconates.
- Electronics business start: the history table lists "電子材料「コロイダルシリカ」の試験生産開始" (trial production of colloidal silica), but the year is not reliably mapped from the converted table [ND].
- 1990s to 2000s: Chinese subsidiary Qingdao Fuso (founded 1994, 30th anniversary in 2024 [D: 07_FUSO-TOPICS]); purchase of the domestic fine-chemicals business and the US subsidiary PMP Fermentation Products from Fujisawa Pharmaceutical (gluconates); Thai subsidiary FUSO (THAILAND).
- Oct-2014: took over Mitsui Chemicals' organic-acid business and began selling maleic anhydride and fumaric acid. This is where the petrochemical (benzene) exposure comes from.
- Nov-2017: opened the Kashima site (Kamisu, Ibaraki, eastern Japan). Jul-2019: malic acid plant completed at Kashima.
- Apr-2022: Prime Market. Apr-2023: Kashima Phase I ultra-high-purity colloidal silica plant completed. Sep-2023: head office moved to Osaka. Oct-2024: Kyoto new silica line. Aug-2025: Kashima Phase II. Mar-2026: decision on the ¥40 bn Kyoto plant. 1-Apr-2026: 3-for-1 split.
- Previous medium-term plan FUSO VISION 2025 (FY03/2022 to FY03/2026): updated May-2023 to sales 850, OP 190, EBITDA-type 300. Outcome: sales 769 (-9.5%), OP 188.5, EBITDA-type 297.8, overseas 55.1% vs 50% target [D: Deck26 P49; Yuho25 P12].

**Why does a fruit-acid company also make semiconductor materials?** The honest answer from the files: a shared site, balance sheet and purification culture, not shared customers or process technology.
- Shared: Kashima hosts maleic anhydride, fumaric, malic and silica plants ("combined production site") [D: MTP P17; IR25 P44]; high-purity organic acids built at Kashima for electronics customers (Oct-2024) bridge both [D: Yuho25 P14, P26]; both segments are "global niche top" businesses managed on pre-depreciation profit.
- Not shared: customers (food/beverage/industrial vs chip-materials formulators), process (fermentation and petrochemical synthesis vs sol-gel silicon chemistry), demand cycle, capital intensity.
- No evidence of commercial cross-selling [ND]. Treat as two businesses under one balance sheet. The listing history also matters: the founding family circle still holds large stakes (section 11).

**Timeline of the electronics and AI-related business**
- Material to profit from FY03/2021 (EM OP 76.5 of 109.6 segment OP, 70%).
- Capex and R&D choices that made it happen: ~¥50 bn in three silica lines over FY03/2022 to FY03/2026 [D: MTP P7]; EM capex FY03/2022 to FY03/2026 = 63.6 bn [Model]; R&D 10.9 oku in FY03/2026 (EM 7.2 oku, LS 3.7 oku) [D: Yuho26 P37].
- Management itself dates the AI lift to FY03/2025 to FY03/2026: "recovery of semiconductor market centered on AI" [D: Yuho25 P14; Rev].

