## 3. What they actually do (company level)

**Products.** Electronic Materials: ultra-high-purity colloidal silica (CMP abrasive and silicon-wafer polishing), hollow submicron silica Miralica™ (low-dielectric fillers; production line under construction for FY03/2027), silica nanopowder (toner external additive), high-purity organosilica sol, alkyl silicate [D: Deck26 P15, P37]. Life Science: malic, citric, gluconic and fumaric acids and salts, maleic anhydride, vitamin C, other fruit acids (succinic, lactic, tartaric), FFA (functional fruit-acid formulations: coated acids, shelf-life improvers, antioxidant and anti-browning agents), high-purity organic acids [D: Deck26 P15; Yuho26 P29-32].

**Customers and sales model.**
- B2B, make-to-forecast: "we produce on expected demand, so order backlog is not tracked" [D: Yuho26 P30].
- EM: sold to slurry formulators and chipmakers after customer qualification (認定) of each production line; one named >10% customer, FUJIFILM Electronic Materials Taiwan: 10,675m yen, 13.9% of group sales (12.9% in FY03/2025) [D: Yuho26 P30, P100]. Taiwan overall 13.7 bn (17.8%), USA 11.7 bn (15.2%) [D: Yuho26 P100]. TSMC N2-generation adoption disclosed [D: Deck26 P30]. Other customers ND. China about 10% of EM sales, guided above 10% for FY03/2026-27 [D: Deck26 P30; Q2deck P31].
- LS: food and beverage makers, detergent and industrial users, pharma/supplement makers; many sales by tender [D: Deck26 P21-22]. Customers ND. Related-party sales to Teikoku Pharmaceutical (65m yen) [D: Yuho26 P103].
- Channel: direct plus overseas subsidiaries (Qingdao, Thailand, PMP); trading houses ND.

**Why customers buy.** EM: purity (99.9999%+), tight particle-size control and lot consistency; "design, supply and quality assurance as one service" [D: MTP P13; IR25 P20-24]. LS: stable supply, domestic fruit-acid capability (rare in Japan), formulation know-how; competition from Chinese low-cost makers is intense [D: MTP P10; Yuho26 P14].

