## 6. AI, PC and smartphone exposure: claim vs evidence

**What Fuso says.** AI semiconductors strong, PC and smartphone weak; AI-driven shipments exceeded plan; adoption for TSMC N2; requirements confirmed for A16/A14, A10 development started; CMP step count rises with multilayer wiring, backside power delivery (BSPDN) and advanced packaging [D: Deck26 P28, P30, P37; MTP P14; Rev].

**Mechanism (why more AI means more silica).**
1. More leading-edge wafers (company and customers) [D: Yuho26 P33].
2. More CMP steps per wafer: multilayer wiring, BSPDN (wafer backside polishing), advanced packaging [D: MTP P14].
3. HBM and hybrid bonding: thicker films to polish (higher removal rate, dense ultra-pure silica) and flatter bonding surfaces (fewer coarse and fine particles); possible new uses: Cu/TSV polishing, Ru and Mo conductors, backside Si, resin layers [D: Deck26 P35]. HBM = stacked DRAM chips linked by through-silicon vias; the extra wafer area and CMP per bit versus conventional DRAM is [I-general], no figure in the folder.
4. Higher spec per tonne: purer, tighter size control, so price erodes less at the leading edge [D: MTP P14; peer analog: Nissan Chemical Q&A].
5. Customer inventory building inflated FY03/2026 volume: "customer usage and inventory increased" [D: Q2deck P32]. Not recurring demand.

**Quantified evidence.** EM sales 415.1 (+25.0%); CMP slurry market volume CAGR 5-6%, value CAGR 6.5% (2025-2030); Fuso EM CAGR 13.2% to FY03/2031; customers' own forecast 8-10% volume CAGR FY03/2025 to FY03/2031; slurry market forecast raised from 3% (Jan-2025) to 6% (Oct-2025) [D: Deck26 P31; MTP P5, P14; Q2deck P30, P32; Yuho26 P33]. WSTS semiconductor market +19.7% (2024), +22.5% (2025), +26.3% (2026F) [D: Deck26 P31].

**What is NOT disclosed [ND]:** share of EM sales that is AI, HBM, logic, DRAM, NAND; volumes in tonnes; price per tonne; customer-by-customer sales other than Fujifilm Taiwan; Fuso's share of the slurry abrasive market.

**Cycle evidence.** FY03/2024: EM sales -19%, OP -44%, margin 30.3% in the 2023 inventory adjustment while Kashima I depreciation started [D: Bilingual P8; Model]. Customers expect AI growth to slow in company-years 2027-28 (FY03/2028-29) [D: Q2deck P32].

**What would make the narrative fail.** AI capex digestion in FY03/2028-29 as new plants arrive; overcapacity at Fuso and peers (Fujimi is also adding CMP capacity [D: Fujimi 01]); customer multi-sourcing, standardization or in-sourcing (the company rates this risk "low" [D: IR25 P24]); abrasive substitution [I-general]; China self-sufficiency; export controls (a Fujimi slide quotes Samsung: HBM sales fell on AI-chip export controls [D: Fujimi 03]); qualification delays at Kashima II or the new Kyoto plant.

