## 9. Unit economics

- **Revenue model.** Volume times price per grade; EM price set by negotiation and cost pass-through; LS by tender and list price. FX: yen per USD 150 assumed; sensitivity per 1 yen = 2.1 oku sales, 0.9 oku OP [D: Deck26 P39].
- **Cost drivers.** EM: metallic silicon, energy (LNG shown on the silicon/LNG slide), depreciation, labor and maintenance of added lines, R&D. LS: benzene (malic, fumaric, maleic), sulfuric acid (citric), fermentation inputs [ND], energy, logistics materials, outsourced products (29% of LS sales) [D: Deck26 P24-25, P28, P36].
- **Gross margin and SG&A.** FY03/2026: gross margin 38.1%, SG&A 13.6% of sales (COGS 47.6 bn, SG&A 10.5 bn); FY03/2025: 37.4% and 14.0% [D: Yuho26 consolidated income statement; I: ratios]. Almost all depreciation sits in cost of sales (+26.2 of +26.3 oku in FY03/2026) [D: Deck26 P8].
- **Operating leverage.** Incremental cash cost per extra sale in FY03/2026 was 20% (CoGS ex-depreciation +14.5 on sales +74.2). Incremental EBITDA-type margin: FY03/2022 36%, FY03/2023 30%, FY03/2025 60%, FY03/2026 71%, FY03/2027 guide 81% [I]. The FY03/2027 bridge shows CoGS ex-depreciation falling 2.7 on sales +88.7 [D: Deck26 P43], which requires price increases to drop through and Kashima II to fill without new fixed cost.
- **Depreciation.** Declining balance (定率法) for Japanese entities, machinery life 4-8 years, buildings 10-50 [D: Yuho26 P75]: front-loaded charges. Kashima II depreciated from Dec-2025. Plan: 109.3 (FY03/2026), 127.0 (FY03/2027), 127.0 (FY03/2028 rough). Implied by the MTP: total D&A ~207 oku in FY03/2031 (567 minus 360) vs 127.0 in FY03/2027 [I].
- **Capital intensity.** EM segment assets 1.75x sales; LS 1.14x; EM segment ROA about 21.9% (FY03/2026) [I]. Cost per unit of silica capacity is about one third higher in the Kyoto project than in the three previous lines (¥133 bn vs ¥100 bn per 1.0x of FY03/2023 capacity) [I, assumptions in Deep-dive 2.5].
- **Working capital.** Mar-2026: receivables 16.6 bn (~79 days of sales), inventories 18.4 bn (finished 14.2, WIP 0.7, raw 3.5; ~141 days of cost of sales) [I: Q1tan P3 comparatives; Tan26]. Q1 FY03/2027: receivables 19.6 bn, inventories 18.3 bn.
- **What capex funds.** About three quarters of capex goes to EM silica lines; LS capex is seismic reinforcement at Osaka, Kashima maintenance and PMP expansions.

