## 14. Tailwinds and headwinds

**Tailwinds**
1. **Leading-edge and AI demand for CMP.** More CMP steps (multilayer wiring, BSPDN, advanced packaging); customers forecast 8-10% volume CAGR; TSMC N2 adoption. Affects EM, whose sales grew 25% in FY03/2026 [D].
2. **Capacity and utilization.** Three new lines (~1.5x FY03/2023 capacity); Kashima I and the Kyoto line at full operation; Kashima II to fill in FY03/2027 [D].
3. **Pricing power.** 5-10% increases agreed with customers from FY03/2027; potential 21-42 oku of the 79 oku EM sales increase [I].
4. **Mix and new products.** High-concentration grades (1.5x), Miralica, toner additives; A16/A14/A10 sampling [D].
5. **Weak yen and overseas growth.** Overseas 55.1%; ¥1 = 0.9 oku OP; China EM above 10% of segment sales [D].
6. **Life Science volumes abroad.** Malic acid overseas +20%, gluconic +10%, FFA cases +30% (China), +20% (Thailand) [D].

**Headwinds**
1. **Depreciation before revenue.** Depreciation 109.3 to 127.0 oku; Kashima II not yet certified (May-2026); Kyoto plant depreciating from 2029 [D/I].
2. **Customer concentration and cycle.** Fujifilm Taiwan about 26% of EM; FY03/2024 showed -44% OP in a destocking year; AI growth expected to slow in FY03/2028-29 [D].
3. **Benzene and Middle East.** Benzene +52% vs FY03/2026 average; maleic anhydride plant restart uncertain in late June 2026; guide excludes it [D].
4. **Competition in Life Science.** Chinese low-cost products; price concessions in fumaric and citric; vitamin C volume -6% index [D].
5. **Tax and non-operating normalization.** Effective tax ~31.7% planned vs 26.7%; FX gains fading [I].
6. **Capital intensity and execution.** Cost per unit of capacity ~33% higher in Kyoto; 299 oku capex in FY03/2027; labor shortage (smart-factory program, pay +30% target) [I; D: Deck26 P34; MTP P5].

