## Appendix B. Benzene and raw materials

- Benzene ACP (USD/t): FY03/2025 average 996; FY03/2026 average 745 (low ~675); Apr-May 2026 1,130 [D: Deck26 P25]. Plan assumes 745 [D: Deck26 P39].
- Disruption (company wording): naphtha distribution cut by Middle East instability; maleic anhydride plant ran on secured raw material until early-May maintenance; restart after late-June maintenance uncertain; external purchase of maleic anhydride under consideration; price correction "a must" if benzene stays high; sulfur disruption lifted sulfuric acid cost (citric acid); packaging and logistics materials short and expensive [D: Deck26 P25].
- Arithmetic (not company data): +385 USD/t x 150 yen = about 57,750 yen per tonne. About 9,200 tonnes a year of benzene would equal 10% of LS operating profit (0.53 bn). Malic acid sold overseas (12,400 t) alone implies roughly 11,000 t of benzene [I-general stoichiometry] and about 0.65 bn gross extra cost before pass-through.
- Mitigations: price revisions, secured raw material, external maleic anhydride, higher in-house share (71% to 75% target: 49% domestic plus 22% overseas in-house, 29% outsourced), higher utilization, government and supplier coordination [D: Deck26 P24-25, P36].
- EM analog: metallic silicon from China-heavy sources; Qingdao subsidiary processes silicon; diversification to Malaysia and Brazil [D: Yuho26 P25; IR25 P44; Deck26 P36].

